    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d780">

                <pb facs="0583" n="579" xml:id="pg579"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11/2117: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-04-16T17:00:00-05:00">April 16, 1938—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>127. Your 196, April 8, 3 p.m. The Department approves your proposed action as
                    outlined in the last sentence of your telegram under reference.</p>
                <p>You will of course bear in mind in this connection the Department’s 262 to
                    Nanking, September 24, 1937, 2 p.m.,<anchor n="20" xml:id="d780-f1"/> and
                    Department’s 14 to Peiping, January 14, 6 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
